      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree she found a curl of stairs going down, and at the very top step sat an old grey fox in a patched green vest. His name was Mosk, and he watched her with eyes like polished stones. He told her, in a voice like dry leaves skittering on a path, that the tree was not for visiting and she should go home and forget the humming. Lina tucked her chin, firm and steady, and said she could not forget what she had not yet heard."
    }
